# D5: the TIMED arm with the quad OFF: D4's tests on c2-packed-tp4-speed-pairs (c2-packed-tp4-speed stated as the -quad profile's pair:
# QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=0, the verify audits off, no draft audit). In concurrent4_steady the four steady users draft as two packed
# pairs (about 24 ms of device time each, one collect and one batched select per round), in concurrent4 (two ramp users) every user
# drafts singly. The difference between D4 and D5 is the quad's saving over the pairs (projected about 7 ms per round, 141 against
# 134 ms), and between D5 and the speed window's K2 the pairs' saving over the singles (projected about 27-31 ms, 170 against 141 ms):
# the measurement that calibrates every projection of the drafting diagnosis (R0).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card batched-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image D0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min; tests 10-15 min: 15 / 30 / 70 min.
# Read: as D4 with the pairs: '[PACKED-SELECT] round=N pairs=[[0, 1], [2, 3]] users=4' in concurrent4_steady, no quad line, early_draft
# (expect 33-38 ms) and propose in [PHASE], the per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean against D4's (the acceptance must be
# the same: the drafts are the same bits).
# SOFT: the numbers are the product. The smoke step ENFORCES the stop conditions: an errored or empty stream, garbage text, an audit
# mismatch line, no quad line at all, and that at least one round was served by two packed pairs.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-draft-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-pairs
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
